nting"},{"text":"Corporate finance"},{"text":"Risk management"},{"text":"Compliance"},{"text":"Fintech"},{"text":"Legal technology"}]}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After LL.B/Integrated LL.B, suitable options include:"},{"type":"h","text":"LL.M"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential specializations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Banking & Finance Law"},{"text":"Corporate & Commercial Law"},{"text":"Business Law"},{"text":"Financial Law"},{"text":"Corporate Law"},{"text":"Securities Law"},{"text":"Insolvency Law"},{"text":"International Commercial Law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Options"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MBA Finance"},{"text":"MBA Financial Services"},{"text":"Compliance-focused programs"},{"text":"FinTech programs"},{"text":"Corporate governance programs"}]},{"type":"p","text":"An LL.M is not mandatory for becoming a banking lawyer. Strong internships, drafting ability, commercial understanding and relevant work experience can be more important for many entry-level roles."}]},{"heading":"Career Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After gaining experience, a Banking Lawyer can specialize in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Corporate Banking"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Corporate lending"},{"text":"Working capital"},{"text":"Credit facilities"},{"text":"Guarantees"},{"text":"Security documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project Finance"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Infrastructure financing"},{"text":"Energy projects"},{"text":"Transportation"},{"text":"Industrial projects"},{"text":"Public-private projects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Debt Finance"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Debt instruments"},{"text":"Corporate borrowing"},{"text":"Structured financing"},{"text":"Refinancing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Insolvency & Restructuring"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stressed assets"},{"text":"Creditor representation"},{"text":"Restructuring"},{"text":"Insolvency proceedings"}]},{"typ